      content: "धर्मगुब्धर्मकृद्धर्मी सदसत्क्षरमक्षरम्।\nअविज्ञाता सहस्रांशुर्विधाता कृतलक्षणः॥ ५१\n\n489. धर्मगुप् (Dharmagupt) — protector of dharma\n490. धर्मकृत् (Dharmakrit) — performer of dharma\n491. धर्मी (Dharmi) — the embodiment of righteousness\n492. सदसत् (Sadasat) — both being and non-being\n493. क्षरम् (Ksharam) — the perishable\n494. अक्षरम् (Aksharam) — the imperishable\n495. अविज्ञाता (Avijnaata) — not fully known to any\n496. सहस्रांशुः (Sahasramshu) — thousand-rayed like the sun\n497. विधाता (Vidhata) — the cosmic ordainer\n498. कृतलक्षणः (Kritalakshanah) — marked with all auspicious signs\n\nगभस्तिनेमिः सत्त्वस्थः सिंहो भूतमहेश्वरः।\nआदिदेवो महादेवो देवेशो देवभृद्गुरुः॥ ५२\n\n499. गभस्तिनेमिः (Gabhastinemih) — the hub of all cosmic rays\n500. सत्त्वस्थः (Satvasthah) — established in pure sattva\n501. सिंहः (Simhah) — the lion of lions\n502. भूतमहेश्वरः (Bhuta-maheshvarah) — great lord of all beings\n503. आदिदेवः (Aadidevah) — the first and primordial deity\n504. महादेवः (Mahadevah) — the great divine lord\n505. देवेशः (Deveshh) — the supreme lord of all gods\n506. देवभृद्गुरुः (Devabhridguruh) — the teacher who sustains all gods\n\nउत्तरो गोपतिर्गोप्ता ज्ञानगम्यः पुरातनः।\nशरीरभूतभृद्भोक्ता कपीन्द्रो भूरिदक्षिणः॥ ५३\n\n507. उत्तरः (Uttarah) — the ultimate savior\n508. गोपतिः (Gopatih) — lord of cows / senses / speech\n509. गोप्ता (Gopta) — the supreme protector\n510. ज्ञानगम्यः (Gyanagamyah) — reached only through knowledge\n511. पुरातनः (Puratanah) — the most ancient one\n512. शरीरभूतभृत् (Shariirabhutabhrit) — the sustainer of all bodily elements\n513. भोक्ता (Bhokta) — the ultimate enjoyer\n514. कपीन्द्रः (Kapindrah) — lord of the Vanaras (monkey warriors)\n515. भूरिदक्षिणः (Bhuridakshinah) — of infinite, abundant charity\n\nसोमपोऽमृतपः सोमः पुरुजित्पुरुसत्तमः।\nविनयो जयः सत्यसन्धो दाशार्हः सात्त्वतां पतिः॥ ५४\n\n516. सोमपः (Somapah) — the drinker of Soma nectar\n517. अमृतपः (Amritapah) — the drinker of immortal nectar\n518. सोमः (Somah) — the moon / nectar itself\n519. पुरुजित् (Purujit) — conqueror of many\n520. पुरुसत्तमः (Purusattamah) — the highest of all beings\n521. विनयः (Vinayah) — humility personified\n522. जयः (Jayah) — victory itself\n523. सत्यसन्धः (Satyasandhah) — of absolutely true resolve\n524. दाशार्हः (Dasharha) — of the Dasharha lineage (Krishna)\n525. सात्त्वतां पतिः (Saattvataampathi) — lord of the sattvic Satvata devotees\n\nजीवो विनयिता साक्षी मुकुन्दोऽमितविक्रमः।\nअम्भोनिधिरनन्तात्मा महोदधिशयोऽन्तकः॥ ५५\n\n526. जीवः (Jeevah) — the life principle in all beings\n527. विनयिता (Vinayita) — the bestower of humility\n528. साक्षी (Saakshi) — the eternal witness\n529. मुकुन्दः (Mukundah) — the giver of liberation (mukti)\n530. अमितविक्रमः (Amitavikrama) — of immeasurable valor\n531. अम्भोनिधिः (Ambhonidhih) — the ocean / treasure of waters\n532. अनन्तात्मा (Anantaatma) — the infinite, boundless soul\n533. महोदधिशयः (Mahodadhishayah) — reclining on the great ocean\n534. अन्तकः (Antakah) — the destroyer at the end of all\n\nअजो महार्हः स्वाभाव्यो जितामित्रः प्रमोदनः।\nआनन्दो नन्दनो नन्दः सत्यधर्मा त्रिविक्रमः॥ ५६\n\n535. अजः (Ajah) — the unborn, birthless\n536. महार्हः (Maharhah) — supremely worthy\n537. स्वाभाव्यः (Svabhavyah) — naturally excellent\n538. जितामित्रः (Jitamitrah) — conqueror of all enemies\n539. प्रमोदनः (Pramodanah) — the bliss-giver\n540. आनन्दः (Anandah) — pure, absolute bliss\n541. नन्दनः (Nandanah) — the delightful one\n542. नन्दः (Nandah) — the bliss-giving one\n543. सत्यधर्मा (Satyadharma) — the embodiment of true dharma\n544. त्रिविक्रमः (Trivikramah) — the one who strode across three worlds (as Vamana)\n\nमहर्षिः कपिलाचार्यः कृतज्ञो मेदिनीपतिः।\nत्रिपदस्त्रिदशाध्यक्षो महाश्रृङ्गः कृतान्तकृत्॥ ५७\n\n545. महर्षिः (Maharshih) — the great cosmic sage\n546. कपिलाचार्यः (Kapilaacharyah) — the teacher Kapila, sage of Sankhya\n547. कृतज्ञः (Kritajnah) — the grateful, remembering all service\n548. मेदिनीपतिः (Mediniipatih) — lord of the earth\n549. त्रिपदः (Tripadah) — the three-stepped one (Trivikrama)\n550. त्रिदशाध्यक्षः (Tridashaadhyakshah) — overseer of the thirty (gods)\n551. महाश्रृङ्गः (Mahashringah) — the great-horned one (as Matsya fish)\n552. कृतान्तकृत् (Kritantakrit) — the maker of ultimate ends\n\nमहावराहो गोविन्दः सुषेणः कनकाङ्गदी।\nगुह्यो गभीरो गहनो गुप्तश्चक्रगदाधरः॥ ५८\n\n553. महावराहः (Mahavarahah) — the great cosmic boar (Varaha avatar)\n554. गोविन्दः (Govindah) — the finder of the earth / cows / senses\n555. सुषेणः (Sushenah) — of beautiful divine army\n556. कनकाङ्गदी (Kanakaangadi) — wearing golden armlets\n557. गुह्यः (Guhyah) — the hidden mystery\n558. गभीरः (Gabheera) — the profoundly deep\n559. गहनः (Gahana) — the impenetrable\n560. गुप्तः (Guptah) — the well-protected\n561. चक्रगदाधरः (Chakra-gada-dharah) — bearer of discus and mace\n\nवेधाः स्वाङ्गोऽजितः कृष्णो दृढः संकर्षणोऽच्युतः।\nवरुणो वारुणो वृक्षः पुष्कराक्षो महामनाः॥ ५९\n\n562. वेधाः (Vedhah) — the creator\n563. स्वाङ्गः (Svangah) — whose body is his own creation\n564. अजितः (Ajitah) — the unconquered\n565. कृष्णः (Krishnah) — the all-attractive, dark-complexioned divine\n566. दृढः (Dridha) — the immovably firm\n567. संकर्षणः (Sankarshana) — the cosmic puller / Balarama\n568. अच्युतः (Achyutah) — the infallible\n569. वरुणः (Varunah) — the god of waters and cosmic law\n570. वारुणः (Varunah) — son of Varuna\n571. वृक्षः (Vrikshah) — the cosmic tree\n572. पुष्कराक्षः (Pushkarakshah) — lotus-eyed\n573. महामनाः (Mahamanah) — of great, expansive mind\n\nभगवान् भगहाऽऽनन्दी वनमाली हलायुधः।\nआदित्यो ज्योतिरादित्यः सहिष्णुर्गतिसत्तमः॥ ६०\n\n574. भगवान् (Bhagavan) — the possessor of all six divine attributes\n575. भगहा (Bhagaha) — the destroyer of worldly attachments\n576. आनन्दी (Anandi) — the eternally blissful\n577. वनमाली (Vanamali) — wearing the forest flower garland (Vanamala)\n578. हलायुधः (Halayudhah) — bearing the plow (Balarama's weapon)\n579. आदित्यः (Adityah) — the sun / born of Aditi\n580. ज्योतिरादित्यः (Jyotiradityah) — the light of the sun\n581. सहिष्णुः (Sahishnuh) — the supremely patient\n582. गतिसत्तमः (Gatisattamah) — the highest goal of all"
