      content: "679. भ्राजिष्णुः (Bhrajishnuh) — the brilliantly shining one\n680. भोजनम् (Bhojanam) — the food that nourishes all\n681. भोक्ता (Bhokta) — the enjoyer of all\n682. सहिष्णुः (Sahishnuh) — the supremely patient\n683. जगदादिजः (Jagadadijah) — the progenitor of the universe\n684. अनघः (Anaghah) — without sin\n685. विजयः (Vijayah) — victory itself\n686. जेता (Jeta) — the conqueror\n687. विश्वयोनिः (Vishvayonih) — the womb of the universe\n688. पुनर्वसुः (Punarvasuh) — the one who restores again and again\n\nब्रह्मण्यो ब्रह्मकृद् ब्रह्मा ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविवर्धनः।\nब्रह्मविद् ब्रह्मणो ब्रह्मी ब्रह्मज्ञो ब्राह्मणप्रियः॥ ७१\n\n689. ब्रह्मण्यः (Brahmanyah) — one devoted to brahmanas\n690. ब्रह्मकृत् (Brahmakrit) — creator of Brahman knowledge\n691. ब्रह्मा (Brahma) — Brahma the Creator (as Vishnu's manifestation)\n692. ब्रह्म (Brahma) — the Absolute Brahman itself\n693. ब्रह्मविवर्धनः (Brahmavivardhana) — increaser of Brahman realization\n694. ब्रह्मविद् (Brahmavid) — the supreme knower of Brahman\n695. ब्रह्मणः (Brahmanah) — born of Brahman\n696. ब्रह्मी (Brahmi) — in possession of Brahman\n697. ब्रह्मज्ञः (Brahmajnah) — knower of all Brahman wisdom\n698. ब्राह्मणप्रियः (Brahmanapriayah) — the beloved of all brahmanas\n\nमहाक्रमो महाकर्मा महातेजा महोरगः।\nमहाक्रतुर्महायज्वा महायज्ञो महाहविः॥ ७२\n\n699. महाक्रमः (Mahakramah) — of great, vast strides\n700. महाकर्मा (Mahakarmaa) — of great, cosmic deeds\n701. महातेजाः (Mahatejaah) — of supreme, blazing brilliance\n702. महोरगः (Mahoragah) — the great cosmic serpent\n703. महाक्रतुः (Mahakratuh) — the great Vedic ritual\n704. महायज्वा (Mahayajvaa) — the great sacrificer\n705. महायज्ञः (Mahayagnah) — the great sacrifice itself\n706. महाहविः (Mahahavih) — the great oblation\n\nस्तव्यः स्तवप्रियः स्तोत्रं स्तुतिः स्तोता रणप्रियः।\nपूर्णः पूरयिता पुण्यः पुण्यकीर्तिरनामयः॥ ७३\n\n707. स्तव्यः (Stavyah) — supremely worthy of praise\n708. स्तवप्रियः (Stavapriayah) — one who loves to be praised\n709. स्तोत्रम् (Stotram) — the stotra / hymn of praise itself\n710. स्तुतिः (Stutih) — praise itself\n711. स्तोता (Stota) — the one who praises\n712. रणप्रियः (Ranapriayah) — the lover of righteous battle\n713. पूर्णः (Purnah) — the completely full, the perfect\n714. पूरयिता (Porayita) — the one who fills everything\n715. पुण्यः (Punyah) — the supremely holy\n716. पुण्यकीर्तिः (Punyakirtiih) — of supremely holy fame\n717. अनामयः (Anamayah) — forever free from disease\n\nमनोजवस्तीर्थकरो वसुरेता वसुप्रदः।\nवसुप्रदो वासुदेवो वसुर्वसुमना हविः॥ ७४\n\n718. मनोजवः (Manojavah) — swift as thought\n719. तीर्थकरः (Tirthakarah) — creator of all holy tirthas\n720. वसुरेताः (Vasuretah) — the seed of all wealth\n721. वसुप्रदः (Vasupradah) — the bestower of wealth\n722. वासुदेवः (Vasudevah) — the son of Vasudeva\n723. वसुः (Vasuh) — the dwelling in all / the wealth\n724. वसुमनाः (Vasumana) — of a pure and wealthy mind\n725. हविः (Havih) — the oblation offered in sacrifice\n\nसद्गतिः सत्कृतिः सत्ता सद्भूतिः सत्परायणः।\nशूरसेनो यदुश्रेष्ठः सन्निवासः सुयामुनः॥ ७५\n\n726. सद्गतिः (Sadgatih) — the path of the good, the true path\n727. सत्कृतिः (Satkritih) — divine, dharmic action\n728. सत्ता (Satta) — pure existence itself\n729. सद्भूतिः (Sadbhutih) — of noble, pure being\n730. सत्परायणः (Satparayanah) — devoted to the ultimate good\n731. शूरसेनः (Shurasena) — of heroic armies\n732. यदुश्रेष्ठः (Yadushreshtha) — the best of the Yadu clan\n733. सन्निवासः (Sannivasah) — the abode of all the good\n734. सुयामुनः (Suyamuna) — the one by the sacred Yamuna\n\nभूतावासो वासुदेवः सर्वासुनिलयोऽनलः।\nदर्पहा दर्पदो दृप्तो दुर्धरोऽथापराजितः॥ ७६\n\n735. भूतावासः (Bhutavasah) — the dwelling place of all beings\n736. वासुदेवः (Vasudevah) — all-pervading, omnipresent\n737. सर्वासुनिलयः (Sarvaasunilayah) — the abode of all vital breaths\n738. अनलः (Analah) — fire, the eternal\n739. दर्पहा (Darpaha) — the destroyer of pride\n740. दर्पदः (Darpada) — the giver of noble pride\n741. दृप्तः (Dripta) — the supremely exalted\n742. दुर्धरः (Durdharah) — the invincible\n743. अपराजितः (Aparajitah) — the undefeated, unconquerable\n\nविश्वमूर्तिर्महामूर्तिर्दीप्तमूर्तिरमूर्तिमान्।\nअनेकमूर्तिरव्यक्तः शतमूर्तिः शताननः॥ ७७\n\n744. विश्वमूर्तिः (Vishvamurti) — the universal form\n745. महामूर्तिः (Mahamurtih) — of immense, cosmic form\n746. दीप्तमूर्तिः (Diptamurti) — of radiant, blazing form\n747. अमूर्तिमान् (Amurtiman) — the formless\n748. अनेकमूर्तिः (Anekamurti) — of many forms\n749. अव्यक्तः (Avyakta) — the unmanifest\n750. शतमूर्तिः (Shatamurti) — of a hundred forms\n751. शताननः (Shatanana) — of a hundred faces\n\nएको नैकः सवः कः किं यत्तत्पदमनुत्तमम्।\nलोकबन्धुर्लोकनाथो माधवो भक्तवत्सलः॥ ७८\n\n752. एकः (Ekah) — the one, the single\n753. नैकः (Naikah) — the many\n754. सवः (Savah) — the Soma sacrifice\n755. कः (Kah) — who? — Brahma himself\n756. किम् (Kim) — what is he?\n757. यत् (Yat) — that which is\n758. तत् (Tat) — that\n759. पदमनुत्तमम् (Padamuttamam) — the supreme state\n760. लोकबन्धुः (Lokabandhu) — friend of all the worlds\n761. लोकनाथः (Lokanatha) — lord of all the worlds\n762. माधवः (Madhava) — the husband of Lakshmi\n763. भक्तवत्सलः (Bhaktavatsala) — affectionately loving to devotees\n\nसुवर्णवर्णो हेमाङ्गो वराङ्गश्चन्दनाङ्गदी।\nवीरहा विषमः शून्यो घृताशीरचलश्चलः॥ ७९\n\n764. सुवर्णवर्णः (Suvarna-varnah) — of golden hue\n765. हेमाङ्गः (Hemangah) — of golden limbs\n766. वराङ्गः (Varanga) — of supremely beautiful limbs\n767. चन्दनाङ्गदी (Chandanangadi) — wearing sandalwood-scented armlets\n768. वीरहा (Viraha) — the slayer of the valiant\n769. विषमः (Vishamah) — beyond equality, beyond comparison\n770. शून्यः (Shunyah) — the void, pure consciousness\n771. घृताशीः (Ghritashih) — whose blessings are like pure ghee\n772. अचलः (Achalah) — the immovable\n773. चलः (Chalah) — the moving principle\n\nअमानी मानदो मान्यो लोकस्वामी त्रिलोकधृक्।\nसुमेधा मेधजो धन्यः सत्यमेधा धराधरः॥ ८०\n\n774. अमानी (Amani) — without ego or arrogance\n775. मानदः (Manada) — the giver of honor\n776. मान्यः (Manya) — worthy of highest honor\n777. लोकस्वामी (Lokasvami) — the master of all worlds\n778. त्रिलोकधृक् (Trilokdhrik) — the upholder of the three worlds\n779. सुमेधाः (Sumedhah) — of excellent wisdom\n780. मेधजः (Medhajah) — born of the Vedic sacrifice\n781. धन्यः (Dhanyah) — the supremely blessed\n782. सत्यमेधाः (Satyamedha) — of true, divine intelligence\n783. धराधरः (Dharadhara) — the upholder of the earth"
